IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `wsa-charges`

-- Water Services Act 2012 (WA), Part 5 -- the questions people ask, for two seats in one layer (the Q&A layer).
--
-- ROLES. The seat is a parameter: every exported question takes `my role` first ("Which of these describes you"):
--   - the owner of land a licensee provides, or could provide, a water supply, sewerage or drainage service to (the
--     baseline's seat, Chloe and Liam at the Byford house);
--   - the occupier of a home who does not own it, such as a tenant: s 95(3) protects the occupier of a dwelling from
--     being cut off without their agreement, a tenant may be made liable as a measured user (s 124(2)(d)) or for an
--     apportioned share (s 125), and s 129 gives the occupier the say on routine entry.
-- A question about the other role answers `does not arise for you` without reading any other input. The licensee (the
-- water utility), the Economic Regulation Authority, the Registrar and the ombudsman are never seats: what they may or
-- must do appears as what it means for the person asking.
--
-- SITUATIONS (design D8 of the graffiti encoding). Within a role, a question that arises only in a situation takes that
-- situation's fact straight after `my role` and answers `does not arise for you` when it does not hold, reading nothing
-- else. All the situations are the owner's; every question of the occupier arises for every occupier:
--   - `my land is not yet connected to the service`: the s 124(2)(c) charge on unconnected land. FALSE gives does not
--     arise;
--   - `my home is let to a tenant`: s 126(1) when the tenant does not pay. FALSE gives does not arise;
--   - `a previous owner made a written agreement with the licensee about the service`: s 76. FALSE gives does not
--     arise;
--   - `water service charges on my land are overdue`: the amount owed on an overdue bill (s 124(2)(n)). FALSE gives does
--     not arise;
--   - `a water memorial has been lodged on my title and not withdrawn`: s 128(3), (4). FALSE gives does not arise;
--   - `my water supply has been cut off or reduced`: s 95(6), (7). FALSE gives does not arise.
--
-- CONTENT. For the owner, every exported question of the baseline (wsa-charges.l4) is asked by calling its function.
-- The baseline's `I am the owner of the land` (s 73) and `I am the owner for the time being` (s 126(1)) are TRUE by the
-- owner's role, and s 128(3)'s `a memorial has been lodged and not withdrawn` is TRUE by its situation. For the
-- occupier the questions are the same rules asked from the occupier's side, by the same functions.
--
-- No exported question takes a DEONTIC or EVENT input. Edition, scope and findings: NOTES.md.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Water Services Act 2012 (WA) -- the questions people ask`

§§ `Who is asking, and the shape of the answers`

DECLARE Role IS ONE OF
    `I own land with a water, sewerage or drainage service, or a main near it`
    `I live in or occupy a home with a water service but do not own it, such as a tenant`

DECLARE `Yes or no` IS ONE OF
    yes
    no
    `does not arise for you`

DECLARE `Amount` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    amount HAS dollars IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Hours` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `notice of` HAS `hours` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Text answer` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the answer` HAS `text` IS A STRING

DECLARE `Who is liable` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `liable` HAS `who the Act makes liable` IS A `Who the Act makes liable`

DECLARE `My supply` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the supply` HAS `what may be done to it` IS A `What may be done to my supply`

GIVEN `it holds` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`yes if` `it holds` MEANS
    IF `it holds` THEN yes ELSE no

§§ `For the owner`

§§§ `What I may be charged, and my entitlement (ss 73, 123, 124(2)(c))`

@export Who may charge me for water services to my home, and on what footing (s 123)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the item` IS A `What I am being asked to pay` @desc What the item on your bill is for
GIVETH A `Text answer`
`Who may charge me, as owner` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land with a water, sewerage or drainage service, or a main near it` THEN `the answer` (`Who may charge me for this` `the item`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Am I, as owner, entitled to have the water service provided to my land (s 73)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `statutory charges apply to my land for the service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether charges under the regulations apply to your land for this service (water supply, sewerage or drainage)
      `the charges due have been paid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the charges for the service that are already due to the licensee have been paid
      `I am keeping to the terms and conditions of the service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are complying with the terms and conditions of the service (the licensee's standard terms, or your agreement)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Am I entitled to the service, as owner` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land with a water, sewerage or drainage service, or a main near it` THEN
        `yes if` (`Am I entitled to the water service` TRUE `statutory charges apply to my land for the service` `the charges due have been paid` `I am keeping to the terms and conditions of the service`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Can I be charged for a water service my land is not yet connected to (s 124(2)(c))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my land is not yet connected to the service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your land is not yet connected to the licensee's works for this service (for example a new lot with the main at the boundary)
      `the regulations apply this charge to unconnected land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the regulations (not deposited) say this charge applies to land not connected to the works
      `connection is practicable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is practicable to connect your land, for example because the main runs within, at or near your boundary
      `my land benefits from the service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your land benefits from the service
      `my land contributes to the need for the service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your land contributes to the need for the service
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can I be charged before I am connected` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land with a water, sewerage or drainage service, or a main near it` THEN
        IF NOT `my land is not yet connected to the service`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Can I be charged for a service I am not connected to` `the regulations apply this charge to unconnected land` `connection is practicable` `my land benefits from the service` `my land contributes to the need for the service`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `Who is liable, and the previous owner (ss 76, 124(2)(d), 125, 126)`

@export Can the unpaid water charges on this land be recovered from me as its owner, even if they arose before I owned it (s 126(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the charge` IS A `Kind of charge` @desc What kind of charge it is: statutory (under the regulations), an alternative charge in an agreement replacing a statutory one, a charge under an agreement where no statutory charge applies, or an incidental charge
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can unpaid charges be recovered from me as owner` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land with a water, sewerage or drainage service, or a main near it` THEN
        `yes if` (`Can the unpaid charges on my land be recovered from me as owner` `the charge` TRUE)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Who is liable for the water charges on my home: me as owner, or my tenant (ss 124(2)(d), 125, 126(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the regulations make the tenant liable for measured use` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the regulations (not deposited) make a person who is not otherwise liable, such as a tenant, liable for a charge because their use is measured
      `the licensee has apportioned the charges between dwellings on one connection` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the home is one of 2 or more dwellings on a single property connection and the licensee has apportioned the charges between their owners or occupiers (s 125)
GIVETH A `Who is liable`
`Who is liable, as owner` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land with a water, sewerage or drainage service, or a main near it` THEN
        `liable` (`Who is liable for the water charges on my home` `the regulations make the tenant liable for measured use` `the licensee has apportioned the charges between dwellings on one connection`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export If my tenant is also liable but does not pay, can the statutory charges still be recovered from me (s 126(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my home is let to a tenant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you let the land, or a home on it, to a tenant
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can the charges be recovered from me if my tenant does not pay` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land with a water, sewerage or drainage service, or a main near it` THEN
        IF NOT `my home is let to a tenant`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Can the charges still be recovered from me if my tenant does not pay` TRUE)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Am I, as a later owner, bound by a term of an agreement the previous owner made with the licensee (s 76)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `a previous owner made a written agreement with the licensee about the service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an earlier owner of the land made a written agreement with the licensee about the service to the land
      `the term` IS A `Term of the earlier agreement` @desc What the term of the earlier written agreement is about
      `days before I took possession that a notification was registered` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days before you obtained possession a notification of the agreement was registered or endorsed on the title (0 if none)
      `I otherwise had prior notice of the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you knew of the agreement before you became owner, apart from registration
      `the agreement says it does not bind later owners` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the agreement itself provides that it does not bind later owners
      `I have made my own agreement about the service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have since entered into your own agreement with the licensee about the service, or the service is no longer required
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Am I bound by the earlier owner's agreement` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land with a water, sewerage or drainage service, or a main near it` THEN
        IF NOT `a previous owner made a written agreement with the licensee about the service`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Am I bound by the previous owner's agreement` `the term` `days before I took possession that a notification was registered` `I otherwise had prior notice of the agreement` `the agreement says it does not bind later owners` `I have made my own agreement about the service`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `Unpaid charges and my title (ss 124(2)(n), 128)`

@export Can the licensee lodge a memorial on my title for what I owe (s 128(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `what is unpaid` IS A `What is unpaid` @desc What, if anything, is unpaid on the land
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can a memorial be lodged on my title` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land with a water, sewerage or drainage service, or a main near it` THEN
        `yes if` (`Can the licensee lodge a memorial on my title` `what is unpaid`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Can a sale, mortgage or other dealing with my land be registered while a water memorial stands (s 128(3))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `a water memorial has been lodged on my title and not withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the licensee has lodged a memorial against your land for unpaid charges that has not been withdrawn
      `my instrument was lodged after the memorial` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the transfer, mortgage or other instrument was lodged for registration after the memorial
      `the licensee has consented in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the licensee has given its written consent to registration
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can my dealing be registered while the memorial stands` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land with a water, sewerage or drainage service, or a main near it` THEN
        IF NOT `a water memorial has been lodged on my title and not withdrawn`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Can my dealing be registered despite a memorial` TRUE `my instrument was lodged after the memorial` `the licensee has consented in writing`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Once I have paid, must the licensee withdraw the memorial (s 128(4))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `a water memorial has been lodged on my title and not withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the licensee has lodged a memorial against your land for unpaid charges that has not been withdrawn
      `the charge or contribution has been paid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the arrears the memorial was lodged for have been paid
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must the memorial be withdrawn` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land with a water, sewerage or drainage service, or a main near it` THEN
        IF NOT `a water memorial has been lodged on my title and not withdrawn`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Must the licensee withdraw the memorial` `the charge or contribution has been paid`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export How much do I owe on an overdue water bill (s 124(2)(n))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `water service charges on my land are overdue` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether any water service charges on your land are unpaid after their due date
      `the unpaid charges` IS A NUMBER @desc The water service charges still unpaid, in dollars
      `interest on the overdue amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The interest the regulations charge on the overdue amount, in dollars (0 if none)
      `late payment penalty` IS A NUMBER @desc Any penalty the regulations impose for late payment, in dollars (0 if none)
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`How much do I owe when overdue` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land with a water, sewerage or drainage service, or a main near it` THEN
        IF NOT `water service charges on my land are overdue`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE amount (`How much do I owe on an overdue bill` `the unpaid charges` `interest on the overdue amount` `late payment penalty`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `My supply (ss 77, 79, 95, 129)`

@export Can my water supply be cut off or reduced (s 95(1)-(4))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `days the charges have been unpaid since falling due` IS A NUMBER @desc Days since the due date that water service charges (with interest) have remained unpaid (0 if nothing is overdue)
      `the land is unoccupied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the land is unoccupied
      `a meter installation has been refused` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the occupier (or the owner, if no occupier) has refused to let a meter be installed
      `the owner has asked for it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the owner has asked the licensee to cut off or reduce the supply
      `the licensee is satisfied a reduction is needed to prevent waste` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the licensee is satisfied a reduction in flow is necessary to prevent the waste of water on the land
      `there is an occupied dwelling on the land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the supply goes to a dwelling that is occupied
      `the occupier agrees to being cut off` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the occupier has agreed to the supply being cut off
      `the licence forbids it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the terms and conditions of the licensee's licence restrict cutting off or reducing in this case
GIVETH A `My supply`
`Can my supply be cut off, as owner` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land with a water, sewerage or drainage service, or a main near it` THEN
        `the supply` (`Can my water be cut off or reduced` `days the charges have been unpaid since falling due` `the land is unoccupied` `a meter installation has been refused` `the owner has asked for it` `the licensee is satisfied a reduction is needed to prevent waste` `there is an occupied dwelling on the land` `the occupier agrees to being cut off` `the licence forbids it`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export If my water is cut off or reduced, does that end what I owe (s 95(6))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my water supply has been cut off or reduced` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the licensee has cut off or reduced the water supply to your land
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Does being cut off end my debt` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land with a water, sewerage or drainage service, or a main near it` THEN
        IF NOT `my water supply has been cut off or reduced`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` `Does being cut off end what I owe`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What can I be required to pay before my water is restored (s 95(7))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my water supply has been cut off or reduced` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the licensee has cut off or reduced the water supply to your land
      `the unpaid charges with interest` IS A NUMBER @desc The unpaid water service charges, with interest on overdue amounts, in dollars
      `the prescribed disconnection and restoration fees` IS A NUMBER @desc The prescribed fees for cutting off or reducing and for restoring the supply (regulations not deposited), in dollars
      `the licensee has accepted a payment arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have made arrangements for payment that the licensee is satisfied with
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What must I pay to have my water restored` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land with a water, sewerage or drainage service, or a main near it` THEN
        IF NOT `my water supply has been cut off or reduced`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE amount (`What must I pay before my water is restored` `the unpaid charges with interest` `the prescribed disconnection and restoration fees` `the licensee has accepted a payment arrangement`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Can I claim from the licensee for loss caused by an interruption to my water service (s 77(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `it resulted from the licensee's negligence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the interruption resulted from a negligent act or omission of the licensee
      `it resulted from the licensee's bad faith` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the interruption resulted from an act or omission of the licensee in bad faith
      `the licensee agreed to be liable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the licensee has agreed to be liable for such loss
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can I claim for an interruption, as owner` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land with a water, sewerage or drainage service, or a main near it` THEN
        `yes if` (`Can I claim for loss from an interruption` `it resulted from the licensee's negligence` `it resulted from the licensee's bad faith` `the licensee agreed to be liable`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Is my meter, and the licensee's certificate of its readings, presumed correct (s 79(1), (2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `there is evidence the meter or reading is wrong` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether there is evidence that the meter is outside tolerance or the reading is wrong
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is the meter presumed correct, as owner` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land with a water, sewerage or drainage service, or a main near it` THEN
        `yes if` (`Is my meter presumed correct` `there is evidence the meter or reading is wrong`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export How many hours' notice must I be given before the licensee's people come onto my land (s 129(2), (5))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the purpose` IS A `Why they want to come in` @desc Why the licensee's authorised person wants to enter
      `it is likely to disrupt the occupants` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the routine inspection or maintenance is likely to cause disruption to the occupants
      `the occupier agreed to less notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the occupier has agreed otherwise
GIVETH A `Hours`
`How much notice before entry, as owner` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land with a water, sewerage or drainage service, or a main near it` THEN
        `notice of` (`How many hours notice must I get before entry` `the purpose` `it is likely to disrupt the occupants` `the occupier agreed to less notice`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `Hardship, concessions and disputes (ss 27, 68, 69, 124(2)(o), 222(2)(c))`

@export What does the Act give me if I am in financial hardship and cannot pay my water charges (s 27(3)(e), (4))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
GIVETH A `Text answer`
`What do I get in hardship, as owner` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land with a water, sewerage or drainage service, or a main near it` THEN `the answer` `What does the Act give me in financial hardship`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Am I entitled to an exemption, discount, rebate or concession on my water charges (ss 124(2)(o), 222(2)(c))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `what the regulations give me` IS A `What the regulations give me` @desc What the regulations (not deposited) make available to you
GIVETH A `Text answer`
`Am I entitled to a concession, as owner` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land with a water, sewerage or drainage service, or a main near it` THEN `the answer` (`Am I entitled to a concession on my water charges` `what the regulations give me`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Can I take my dispute with the water provider to the water services ombudsman, free of charge (ss 3(1), 66(2)(g), 68, 69(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the licensee provides me water services or I am entitled to them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the licensee provides water services to you, or you are entitled to them
      `I am a member of the licensee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a member of the licensee (a cooperative)
      `I am affected by its service or failure to provide one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are affected by the licensee's provision of, or failure to provide, a water service
      `a court or tribunal has dealt with or is dealing with it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a court or tribunal has dealt with, or is dealing with, the matter
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can I go to the ombudsman, as owner` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land with a water, sewerage or drainage service, or a main near it` THEN
        `yes if` (`Can I take my dispute to the water ombudsman` `the licensee provides me water services or I am entitled to them` `I am a member of the licensee` `I am affected by its service or failure to provide one` `a court or tribunal has dealt with or is dealing with it`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§ `For the occupier who does not own the home`

-- Every question here arises for every occupier, so none takes a situation input.

@export Who may charge me for the water services to the home I occupy, and on what footing (s 123)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the item` IS A `What I am being asked to pay` @desc What the item on your bill is for
GIVETH A `Text answer`
`Who may charge me, as occupier` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I live in or occupy a home with a water service but do not own it, such as a tenant` THEN `the answer` (`Who may charge me for this` `the item`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Am I liable for the water charges on the home I occupy, or is the owner (ss 124(2)(d), 125, 126(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the regulations make the tenant liable for measured use` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the regulations (not deposited) make a person who is not otherwise liable, such as a tenant, liable for a charge because their use is measured
      `the licensee has apportioned the charges between dwellings on one connection` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the home is one of 2 or more dwellings on a single property connection and the licensee has apportioned the charges between their owners or occupiers (s 125)
GIVETH A `Who is liable`
`Who is liable, as occupier` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I live in or occupy a home with a water service but do not own it, such as a tenant` THEN
        `liable` (`Who is liable for the water charges on my home` `the regulations make the tenant liable for measured use` `the licensee has apportioned the charges between dwellings on one connection`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

-- s 126(1) makes unpaid statutory and alternative charges recoverable "from the owner of the land for the time being",
-- so the baseline's function, asked of someone who is not the owner, answers no for every kind of charge.
@export Can water charges left unpaid on the land be recovered from me under s 126(1), though I am not the owner?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the charge` IS A `Kind of charge` @desc What kind of charge it is: statutory (under the regulations), an alternative charge in an agreement replacing a statutory one, a charge under an agreement where no statutory charge applies, or an incidental charge
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can unpaid charges on the land be recovered from me as occupier` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I live in or occupy a home with a water service but do not own it, such as a tenant` THEN
        `yes if` (`Can the unpaid charges on my land be recovered from me as owner` `the charge` FALSE)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Can the water supply to the home I occupy be cut off or reduced (s 95(1)-(4))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `days the charges have been unpaid since falling due` IS A NUMBER @desc Days since the due date that water service charges (with interest) have remained unpaid (0 if nothing is overdue)
      `the land is unoccupied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the land is unoccupied
      `a meter installation has been refused` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the occupier (or the owner, if no occupier) has refused to let a meter be installed
      `the owner has asked for it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the owner has asked the licensee to cut off or reduce the supply
      `the licensee is satisfied a reduction is needed to prevent waste` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the licensee is satisfied a reduction in flow is necessary to prevent the waste of water on the land
      `there is an occupied dwelling on the land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the supply goes to a dwelling that is occupied
      `the occupier agrees to being cut off` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the occupier has agreed to the supply being cut off
      `the licence forbids it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the terms and conditions of the licensee's licence restrict cutting off or reducing in this case
GIVETH A `My supply`
`Can my supply be cut off, as occupier` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I live in or occupy a home with a water service but do not own it, such as a tenant` THEN
        `the supply` (`Can my water be cut off or reduced` `days the charges have been unpaid since falling due` `the land is unoccupied` `a meter installation has been refused` `the owner has asked for it` `the licensee is satisfied a reduction is needed to prevent waste` `there is an occupied dwelling on the land` `the occupier agrees to being cut off` `the licence forbids it`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Can I claim from the licensee for loss caused by an interruption to the water service to the home I occupy (s 77(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `it resulted from the licensee's negligence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the interruption resulted from a negligent act or omission of the licensee
      `it resulted from the licensee's bad faith` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the interruption resulted from an act or omission of the licensee in bad faith
      `the licensee agreed to be liable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the licensee has agreed to be liable for such loss
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can I claim for an interruption, as occupier` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I live in or occupy a home with a water service but do not own it, such as a tenant` THEN
        `yes if` (`Can I claim for loss from an interruption` `it resulted from the licensee's negligence` `it resulted from the licensee's bad faith` `the licensee agreed to be liable`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Is the meter at the home I occupy, and the licensee's certificate of its readings, presumed correct (s 79(1), (2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `there is evidence the meter or reading is wrong` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether there is evidence that the meter is outside tolerance or the reading is wrong
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is the meter presumed correct, as occupier` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I live in or occupy a home with a water service but do not own it, such as a tenant` THEN
        `yes if` (`Is my meter presumed correct` `there is evidence the meter or reading is wrong`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export How many hours' notice must I be given before the licensee's people come onto the land I occupy (s 129(2), (5))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the purpose` IS A `Why they want to come in` @desc Why the licensee's authorised person wants to enter
      `it is likely to disrupt the occupants` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the routine inspection or maintenance is likely to cause disruption to the occupants
      `the occupier agreed to less notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the occupier has agreed otherwise
GIVETH A `Hours`
`How much notice before entry, as occupier` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I live in or occupy a home with a water service but do not own it, such as a tenant` THEN
        `notice of` (`How many hours notice must I get before entry` `the purpose` `it is likely to disrupt the occupants` `the occupier agreed to less notice`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What does the Act give me if I am in financial hardship and cannot pay the water charges I am liable for (s 27(3)(e), (4))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
GIVETH A `Text answer`
`What do I get in hardship, as occupier` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I live in or occupy a home with a water service but do not own it, such as a tenant` THEN `the answer` `What does the Act give me in financial hardship`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Can I take my dispute with the water provider to the water services ombudsman, free of charge, as an occupier (ss 3(1), 66(2)(g), 68, 69(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the licensee provides me water services or I am entitled to them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the licensee provides water services to you, or you are entitled to them
      `I am a member of the licensee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a member of the licensee (a cooperative)
      `I am affected by its service or failure to provide one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are affected by the licensee's provision of, or failure to provide, a water service
      `a court or tribunal has dealt with or is dealing with it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a court or tribunal has dealt with, or is dealing with, the matter
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can I go to the ombudsman, as occupier` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I live in or occupy a home with a water service but do not own it, such as a tenant` THEN
        `yes if` (`Can I take my dispute to the water ombudsman` `the licensee provides me water services or I am entitled to them` `I am a member of the licensee` `I am affected by its service or failure to provide one` `a court or tribunal has dealt with or is dealing with it`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`
